      "id": "UQC-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-unitary-quotient-lattices",
      "title": "Finite adelic lattice classes and their rational stabilizers",
      "statement": "For H=U(h) there is a compact open K in its finite adelic group for which the rational double classes are finite. The rational isometries preserving the slice tK are exactly those preserving the lattice L(t).",
      "hypotheses": "A nondegenerate finite-dimensional Hermitian space over the CM extension E/F, its rational unitary group, and integral cores in fixed finite coordinates. Bounded dual index, bounded-basis reduction and reduction adapted to an isotropic line are used.",
