    {
      "id": "UQC-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-unitary-quotient-slices",
      "title": "Finite archimedean domains assemble into one adelic domain",
      "statement": "For representatives t of the finitely many double classes, the union of rectangles D_t × tK is an adelic fundamental domain, with product-Haar measure μ_f(K) times the sum of the archimedean domain measures.",
      "hypotheses": "The countable diagonal subgroup acts faithfully through its archimedean projection. Each archimedean slice stabilizer has a finite-measure fundamental domain. K is compact and open and Haar measures are left invariant.",
